      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Good example is like monthly or yearly challenges of some game ranking lists.  The creator or master of the game challenge might want reset it.\n\nAnother example is game developing. Through the game developing it's very possible some data is not more needed or invalid. Then a whole reset is needed to ensure game save data is good in new game update.\n\nRight now creator must make somewhere erase code so every time player login will get message the save data is reset at the date point. And player date point or version point need saved too, which is extra data.\n\nOnly creator or whitelisted organizer may have rights to erase all data of the game in the world. This can checked by world owner id or organizer name.\n\nSo yeah, this feature is needed.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
